# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for driving this NIF.
#
# beam.smp is not built with TSan, so TSan cannot see the synchronisation inside
# it. The one place that matters here is enif_release_resource: a resource is
# built on one scheduler thread and its destructor runs on whichever thread
# drops the last reference, and the happens-before edge between those two lives
# in the emulator's refcount, which is invisible. Every construct-then-destruct
# of a resource therefore looks like a race between the constructor's writes and
# the destructor's reads.
#
# This suppresses that pair and nothing else. It is deliberately narrow: it names
# the destructors, so a race inside any other function still reports, and the
# check that it has not been widened into uselessness is scripts/run_sanitizer.sh
# with a deliberately reintroduced race, which still fires with this in place.
race:NifResLiteRtCompiledModel::destruct_resource
race:NifResLiteRtEnvironment::destruct_resource
